IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cons54-nouns`
IMPORT `cons54-cross-references`

-- Row il-54. EXPECTED RED: six assertions, all failing, two about each of the three defects. The count (6) is declared in check.sh and in encoding.json.
-- Each states what the citing words need. Nothing here is edited to make it pass.
-- Defect 1: section 31א(א)(7) cites "סעיף 18א(5)", with no letter for the subsection. Since Sefer HaChukim 2159 (26.6.2008) the section's old text is subsection (א) and others follow, so the bare number finds two paragraphs
-- (the second added by Sefer HaChukim 2310, p. 1022) and no paragraph at the top level. Read in context the words reach the warranty-certificate paragraph, and that reading is a green test in cons54-tests-xrefs.l4 (fork F1 in NOTES.md).
-- Defect 2: section 31א(א)(8) cites "סעיף 18א(1)", the same defect: at least three paragraphs carry the number (limb (b) is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY).
-- Defect 3: the Ninth Schedule, item 6, uses the short name "חוק התקשורת". Section 105 of the Communications (Broadcasts) Law, 5786-2026, rewrites the definition in item 1 of the Second Schedule and the use in the Third Schedule,
-- and not the Ninth. The Ninth Schedule starts by 22 July 2027 at the latest and the rewrite on 28 July 2028 (both computed by this row, fork D2), so for a stretch the words reach their definition and after it they do not.
-- The day asked about is well after the rewrite.

§ `Defect 1: a bare paragraph number that two paragraphs carry`

-- 1. What the citing words are about is not what the bare address finds.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 31א(א)(7) to 18א(5), the warranty certificate`)
-- 2. The bare address does not still find one paragraph on a day long after the lettering took effect.
#ASSERT `the words still reach their text on` (`reference: s 31א(א)(7) to 18א(5), the warranty certificate`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Defect 2: a bare paragraph number that at least three paragraphs carry`

-- 3. The same, for 31א(א)(8) and the paragraph on repair and replacement.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 31א(א)(8) to 18א(1), the repair and replacement`)
-- 4. The same day.
#ASSERT `the words still reach their text on` (`reference: s 31א(א)(8) to 18א(1), the repair and replacement`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Defect 3: a short name that the Second Schedule no longer defines`

-- 5. What the citing words are about is not what the Second Schedule defines once section 105 has taken effect.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: Ninth Schedule item 6 to the short name the Second Schedule defines`)
-- 6. The short name does not still reach its definition on a day after the rewrite (1 January 2030).
#ASSERT `the words still reach their text on` (`reference: Ninth Schedule item 6 to the short name the Second Schedule defines`) (Date 1 1 2030) EQUALS JUST TRUE
